FIND_LOWER_BOUND(root, target):
    candidate = nil
    curr = root

    while curr
        if curr.val >= target
            curr = curr.left
        else
            curr = curr.right
    
    return candidate

FIND_UPPER_BOUND(root, target):
    candidate = nil
    curr = root

    while curr
        if curr.val <= target
            candidate = curr
            curr = curr.right
        else
            curr = curr.left
    
    return candidate

OS-COUNT-RANGE(T, k1, k2)
    lower = FIND_LOWER_BOUND(T, k1)
    upper = FIND_UPPER_BOUND(T, k2)

    return val[upper] - val[lower] + 1


Time complexity is O(h) where h = log n because we are effectively removing each half of the tree when searching for the bounds. Because we search twice it is effectivelly O(2h). Space complexity is also O(h) because we use recursion stacks
